InputReader reads stdin in 64 KiB chunks and stops when a read comes back short.
This document is 1025 lines of 64 bytes, 65600 bytes in all, so it takes one
full 65536 byte chunk and then a 64 byte one: the second pass through the loop
is what is being pinned.

The 1025 terminating newlines close 1025 lines; the bytes after the last one do
not invent another line.

A document truncated at the buffer boundary would report 1024.
